From 4e62714c59c9a3d937a60e1774e1b7536fac91b0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 14:08:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] feat(sim): the scallop flank reads to the ball diameter,
 between contact passes only
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ridge flank judged a column only within band + 3·tol of two passes,
so on flat ground a cusp was read only to 4·tol past the ball (s ~ 2.9
on an r3 ball at tol 0.1); a wider spacing verified silent. #37 measured
a plain 2r window convicting 11 finish3d verdict fixtures at crowns and
corners.

The flank now reads within one ball diameter (`ridge::reach`) and asks
the cusp's own geometry (`stock_sim::ridge_scan::flank`):
- only the nearest feet count (within max(cell, 3·tol) of the nearest
  distance): a cusp's column stands equally far from both passes;
- one foot per pass, at its nearest point: runs of joined segments,
  merged by closed ring, so a pass curving round a crown or an edge is
  one side, not a fan of chord feet; a free end gives no side;
- each side's ball must touch the part (`Access::touches`): an air or
  skim pass has no contact path to leave a cusp beside.

The M13.8 per-chord `Flank` is retired; `scan.rs` hands the ridge pass
to the new `ridge_scan` module (scan.rs 431 -> 358 lines).

Readings: every finish3d release-lane fixture stays green (88/88) and
every scallop-asserted one reads 0 before and after; a flat raster now
reads its floor point for s = 3.0 .. 5.9 (s = 4: 0.606; before: 0).
The morphed spiral's apex reading drops 0.132 -> 0 (one pass round the
crown). `verify::envelope_verdict_follows_the_stated_tol` now expects the
tol-0.1 cone rings' real cusp (0.085) as the one non-blocking Scallop
note at a 0.01 budget, no envelope verdict as before.

The verifier only judges: no toolpath or posted output changes.

Fixes #212

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
